+### 4.3 list_conversations
+
+A `list_conversations` frame requests one page of the authenticated user's summaries with optional integer `limit` from 1 to 200 and optional `before` containing both an ISO `updatedAt` and a `sessionId`; it has no user id field ([validated by: accepts list requests and rejects invalid limits or incomplete cursors](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L116)).
+
+| Field    | Type   | Required | Description                                     |
+| -------- | ------ | -------- | ----------------------------------------------- |
+| `type`   | string | Yes      | `"list_conversations"`                          |
+| `limit`  | number | No       | Maximum rows in the page, 1–200                 |
+| `before` | object | No       | `{updatedAt: string, sessionId: string}` cursor |
+
+- A request is answered from `ws.userId`, never a user id in the frame, through `SessionStore.listFor(userId, {limit, before})`. Rows are newest first and carry only `sessionId`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt` and `entryCount`, with ISO strings for both times; the request produces no `stream_end` and no unsolicited list is pushed ([validated by: lists only the authenticated user’s newest summaries and passes a composite cursor to the store](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L138)).
+- `transport.history.enabled` is the deployer's opt-in decision to expose this personal metadata to the client; it defaults off. If it is off, or the store has no `listFor`, the answer is `UNSUPPORTED`, never an empty list ([validated by: returns UNSUPPORTED when history is off or the store cannot list](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L175)).
+- A list is answered outside the per-session turn lock, even while a user message is streaming. The client opens a listed conversation by reconnecting with its `sessionId` under `transport.resume`, whose existing ownership check and replay apply ([validated by: answers a list during a turn and lets its selected conversation resume with replay](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L204)).
+
+**GDPR.** A list exposes one authenticated user's conversation metadata, without conversation content or another user's list ([validated by: lists only the authenticated user’s newest summaries and passes a composite cursor to the store](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L138)). The store's retention and erasure policy remains the deployer's responsibility; see #41.
 
